fference and if you type a lot you'll  probably prefer the air the same thing  goes as far as speakers the 14-inch pro  has the best speakers in any laptop of  this size go ahead and take a listen  [Applause]  [Music]  they are shockingly good with a huge  difference in base thanks to dedicated  woofers and if you are somebody that  will constantly be playing music at full  volume you will really enjoy them with  that said if i'm honest i don't think  that there's ever been a time where i  was sitting there wishing that the  speakers sounded better over louder with  the air they sound great and better than  most of laptops that it will end up  replacing of course the 14-inch brought  back the ports which your current laptop  may or may not have i love that magsafe  is back and we have hdmi and a card  reader and if yours has that now i would  kind of just track how often you use  those ports now for me most of the time  i just use usb type c and even though  dongle suck you just have to ask  yourself is it really worth spending  twice as much money to have them built  in instead of buying a cheap  multi-adapter  i've covered many of them in my top  macbook accessories video which i will  link to after the end of this video so  what is something that bugs me and that  is much better with the pro well that's  the webcam the 720p webcam on the  macbook air was an improvement over the  previous intel models thanks to better  processing but i was never really happy  with it because it kind of looked flat  kind of gray and then in darker  environments you get all this noise so i  always wanted it to be better that is  where the 14 inch macbook comes in with  its 1080p webcam that is much better in  low light situations thanks to its  faster aperture and then in the daytime  of course look sharper as well so  definitely if you care about that the 14  inch is better and with the webcams  let's talk about fans because previous  intel macbooks would spin up their fans  when they are working with video  so that would get annoying it would get  loud it'd be disruptive but the new  macbook air is fanless so you don't have  any of those issues now the pro does  have a fan but because of its efficiency  you never really hear it unless you're  pushing it to its limits so both of  these are pretty much silent now some  people may wonder as far as the  performance are you limited by not  having a fan i really push them to the  limits and yes the air can slow down but  it's not significant and not really a  big deal in the real world so what about  performance this might be the biggest  reason that you're considering the pro  instead of the air well i want to  challenge you a little bit and have you  take a second and ask yourself how much  performance do you really need to be  honest in the real world the air has  more than enough performance for almost  everybody because it smoked even the  expensive high-end 16-inch macbooks in  the past there are only a few people who  i would say that actually need the extra  oomph of the 14 inch and for a lot of  those people i would say you need even  more power you should spend even more  money than this base 2 000 model that  we're comparing to the air the extra cpu  performance cores do result in about 27  more multi-core performance which sounds  like a lot that it is but i have to be  honest and say that i have really never  noticed that in regular day-to-day tasks  that is due to the super fast single  core performance which is the same as  the 14-inch airs and that smokes pretty  much any other older laptop now for  tougher cpu tasks like logic music  production we see a similar difference  but for most people once you get to some  level performance that does what you  need you don't really notice anything  extra now for programming the difference  was about 32  and that can be significant if you're  constantly compiling code and that  performance difference will add up but  even the air was noticeably faster than  the previous errors that even cost more  money and were upgraded and of course  when you're actually writing code you're  not going to notice a difference and  somewhat the same thing happens for  photo editing where i didn't really  notice any difference at any of the  times that i edited photos all but one  time when i was working on a project of  over a thousand high-resolution photos  and really the limit was the eight  gigabytes of ram for that one and then  also when you were exporting those  photos it did take a while and i was  wishing that it was a little bit faster  so in that case if you're somebody  that's going to edit high amounts of  images make sure you at least upgrade to  16 gigs of ram and then see what else  might be worth it as far as the extras  with the 14 inch because then you might  want to upgrade but for most people even  doing photo editing the base model will  not be a limitation but where we start  to see a big difference is graphics  performance for gaming the pro gets  about double the frame rate as it should  having twice as many cores but nobody  really buys a mac for games at least you  definitely shouldn't when it comes to  using those graphics to speed up  productivity we have an overall  improvement of about 80  which is huge but once again a lot of  that is used for regular tasks and this  thing is just still very snappy it's  really only when you get to things like  3d rendering where everything will be  faster loading up your project  running shaders and then of course  rendering your project and you might  think that that is also the case for  video editing but this is where it can  be a little bit tricky if you're using  good software like final cut or resolve  and you're even working with 4k files  with minor effects you literally might  not notice any difference as long as the  graphics is powerful enough to handle  the workload even exporting will be  almost identical because of the same  rendering engines it's really only where  you hit this mac  with a lot of stuff like raw or heavy  effects or for example prores where you  start seeing a big difference because of  the dedicated pro res hardware and once  again that is where i would say you  should actually not get the base model  at least upgrade to the unbid version or  maybe even the m1 max because that will  make a much bigger difference the issue  is though that most people don't need  that amount of performance and people  really get stuck in the kind of thinking  where it's like what if i will need that  what if i'll need that a couple of years  from now and i would just say don't do  that that is marketing and that's how  you get stuck into spending double the  amount of money for a machine where  you're not going to use even half of  what it can offer and as far as future  proofing i think you're better off  buying a base model like this and then  if you need a performance you could sell  it and the resale is amazing on these  base lower price max and then at that  point you could buy whatever is the  latest and greatest and get a better  machine than what this 14-inch offers  today i think that is the better  financial decision and better overall  now the last things we have to cover are  battery life and the displays even  though the air has a smaller battery it  gets significantly better battery life  because of its more efficient processor  and graphics without having a fan and  because its display uses a lot less  power a huge part of the extra price tag  comes from the new mini led xdr display  that is capable of hitting up to 1600  nits instead of 400. now this was the  most attracting exciting thing for me  with these new macbooks other than the  performance but after three months of  use i have to say that for most regular  people it should not be as big of a deal  as apple would want you to think it is  yeah it is better especially if you  watch hdr movies in dark rooms and if  you are editing hdr photos or video you  do absolutely need that kind of a  display but the truth is that i mostly  use my mac with sdr content regular  websites in regular lighting and in  those scenarios it is very hard to tell  the difference side by side yes the 14  inch screen with that notch is  noticeably bigger and i do enjoy it but  unless you're gonna make the most out of  its capabilities it won't be as big of a  deal as apple made it seem at their  event and that actually paints a good  overall picture for the 14 inch macbook  pro how much of it will you make use of  and if you're only attracted to one or  two things say the ports and maybe the  better webcam i don't think that's  enough to justify the extra price point  if you see yourself looking at a macbook  air and saying i'm gonna upgrade the ram  and i also want that webcam i want  better speakers i will use the ports  consistently i need some of that extra  performance and all those extra benefits  start stacking up that's where i would  say you know what make the extra jump  and then spend the extra money but for  most people even though the pro is a  powerful class-leading machine the air  gets a job done and it does so very very  well  and it actually gets my topic in this  comparison for at least 90 to 95 of you  out there this is my recommendation  while it might seem a little bit  outdated it's not the latest and  greatest it is a phenomenal laptop and  for the price point it is the closest  thing to a perfect laptop that has ever  existed yes that is not good i'll go  ahead and link it down below you guys  don't have to buy through there but  there are some great deals on amazon and  also this one as well if you guys want  to pick it up and whichever one you  choose for uh choose to get check out  that video right over there i have the  best macbook accessories and you guys  can click above to help us reach our  goal of 1 million subscribers we  definitely appreciate it that's been max  and i will see you in the next video  [Music]

